<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palamede Gattilusio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1455">1455</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palamede <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gattilusio">Gattilusio</a> was a Genoese lord of Ainos (Enez) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, from the Gattilusio family that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a> and other northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> lands under Byzantine suzerainty. He ruled from 1409 until his death in 1455, and inscriptions and fortifications of his time survive at Enez and on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samothrace">Samothrace</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took Ainos in 1456, soon after his death.</p></div>
